{"id":"mahabharata-4-052","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":52,"title":"द्विपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 52 · Arjuna defeats Kripa","summary":{"en":"Kripa attacks and the two exchange showers of arrows; Arjuna cuts Kripa's bow again and again, kills his horses and charioteer and shatters his chariot. Kripa fights on foot until the Kaurava warriors carry him away from the field.","kn":"ಕೃಪನು ಆಕ್ರಮಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ಬಾಣಮಳೆಗರೆಯುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಕೃಪನ ಧನುಸ್ಸನ್ನು ಮತ್ತೆ ಮತ್ತೆ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿ ಕುದುರೆ ಸಾರಥಿಯರನ್ನು ಕೊಂದು ರಥ ಪುಡಿಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕೌರವವೀರರು ಹೊತ್ತೊಯ್ಯುವವರೆಗೆ ಕೃಪನು ಕಾಲ್ನಡಿಗೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कृप आक्रमण करते हैं और दोनों बाणों की वर्षा करते हैं; अर्जुन बार-बार कृप का धनुष काटते हैं, उनके घोड़े और सारथि मारते हैं और रथ चूर कर देते हैं। कौरव योद्धाओं के उन्हें रणभूमि से ले जाने तक कृप पैदल लड़ते रहते हैं।","te":"కృపుడు దాడి చేస్తాడు, ఇద్దరూ బాణవర్షం కురిపిస్తారు; అర్జునుడు కృపుని ధనుస్సును మళ్లీ మళ్లీ నరికి గుర్రాలను, సారథిని చంపి రథాన్ని ధ్వంసం చేస్తాడు. కౌరవవీరులు తీసుకువెళ్లే వరకు కృపుడు కాలినడకన పోరాడతాడు.","ta":"க்ருபர் தாக்க, இருவரும் அம்பு மழை பொழிகிறார்கள்; அர்ஜுனன் க்ருபரின் வில்லை மீண்டும் மீண்டும் முறித்து, குதிரைகளையும் தேரோட்டியையும் கொன்று தேரை நொறுக்குகிறான். கௌரவ வீரர்கள் அவரைக் களத்திலிருந்து தூக்கிச் செல்லும் வரை க்ருபர் கால்நடையாகப் போரிடுகிறார்.","ml":"കൃപർ ആക്രമിക്കുകയും ഇരുവരും അമ്പുമഴ പെയ്യിക്കുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു. അർജുനൻ കൃപരുടെ വില്ല് പലതവണ മുറിക്കുകയും, കുതിരകളെയും സാരഥിയെയും കൊല്ലുകയും, രഥം തകർക്കുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു. കൗരവയോദ്ധാക്കൾ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ രണഭൂമിയിൽനിന്ന് കൊണ്ടുപോകുന്നതുവരെ കൃപർ കാലാൾ ആയി പൊരുതുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.52; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"गोग्रहणपर्व","titleEn":"Gograhana Parva (The cattle raid)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एतस्मिन्नन्तरे तत्र महावीर्यपराक्रमः ।\nआजगाम महासत्त्वः कृपः शस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nअर्जुनं प्रति संयोद्धुं युद्धार्थी स महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meanwhile the mighty and valiant Kripa, best of weapon-bearers, a great charioteer eager for battle, came there to fight Arjuna."}},{"n":2,"text":"तौ रथौ सूर्यसंकाशौ योत्स्यमानौ महाबलौ ।\nशारदाविव जीमूतौ व्यरोचेतां व्यवस्थितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two mighty chariots, bright as the sun and ready to fight, stood out like two autumn clouds."}},{"n":3,"text":"पार्थोऽपि विश्रुतं लोके गाण्डीवं परमायुधम् ।\nविकृष्य चिक्षेप बहून्नाराचान्मर्मभेदिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha drew the Gandiva, his supreme and world-famous weapon, and shot many arrows that pierce vital parts."}},{"n":4,"text":"तानप्राप्ताञ्शितैर्बाणैर्नाराचान्रक्तभोजनान् ।\nकृपश्चिच्छेद पार्थस्य शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa cut those blood-drinking arrows with his sharp shafts before they reached him, by the hundred and then the thousand."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः पार्थश्च संक्रुद्धश्चित्रान्मार्गान्प्रदर्शयन् ।\nदिशः संछादयन्बाणैः प्रदिशश्च महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the furious Partha, showing varied paths of shooting, covered the directions and in-between directions with arrows."}},{"n":6,"text":"एकच्छायमिवाकाशं प्रकुर्वन्सर्वतः प्रभुः ।\nप्रच्छादयदमेयात्मा पार्थः शरशतैः कृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Making the sky seem all one shade, the immeasurable Partha covered Kripa with hundreds of arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"स शरैरर्पितः क्रुद्धः शितैरग्निशिखोपमैः ।\nतूर्णं शरसहस्रेण पार्थमप्रतिमौजसम् ।\nअर्पयित्वा महात्मानं ननाद समरे कृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced by those sharp arrows like tongues of flame, Kripa, angry, quickly pierced the matchless Partha with a thousand arrows and roared in battle."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः कनकपुङ्खाग्रैर्वीरः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nत्वरन्गाण्डीवनिर्मुक्तैरर्जुनस्तस्य वाजिनः ।\nचतुर्भिश्चतुरस्तीक्ष्णैरविध्यत्परमेषुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the hero Arjuna, hurrying, with gold-tipped, smooth-jointed arrows shot from the Gandiva, struck his four horses with four keen, excellent arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"ते हया निशितैर्विद्धा ज्वलद्भिरिव पन्नगैः ।\nउत्पेतुः सहसा सर्वे कृपः स्थानादथाच्यवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced by those sharp shafts like blazing snakes, the horses suddenly leapt up and Kripa was thrown from his place."}},{"n":10,"text":"च्युतं तु गौतमं स्थानात्समीक्ष्य कुरुनन्दनः ।\nनाविध्यत्परवीरघ्नो रक्षमाणोऽस्य गौरवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Gautama thrown from his place, the delight of the Kurus, killer of enemy heroes, did not strike him, out of respect."}},{"n":11,"text":"स तु लब्ध्वा पुनः स्थानं गौतमः सव्यसाचिनम् ।\nविव्याध दशभिर्बाणैस्त्वरितः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having regained his place, Gautama quickly pierced Savyasachin with ten heron-feathered arrows."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततः पार्थो धनुस्तस्य भल्लेन निशितेन च ।\nचिच्छेदैकेन भूयश्च हस्ताच्चापमथाहरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha cut his bow in half with a sharp spear-arrow and, once more, snatched the bow from his hand."}},{"n":13,"text":"अथास्य कवचं बाणैर्निशितैर्मर्मभेदिभिः ।\nव्यधमन्न च पार्थोऽस्य शरीरमवपीडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha shattered his armor with sharp, vital-piercing arrows, but did not harm Kripa's body."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्य निर्मुच्यमानस्य कवचात्काय आबभौ ।\nसमये मुच्यमानस्य सर्पस्येव तनुर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the armor fell from him, his body shone like a snake's body when it sheds its skin in season."}},{"n":15,"text":"छिन्ने धनुषि पार्थेन सोऽन्यदादाय कार्मुकम् ।\nचकार गौतमः सज्यं तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Partha cut his bow, Gautama took up another and strung it, which seemed a wonder."}},{"n":16,"text":"स तदप्यस्य कौन्तेयश्चिच्छेद नतपर्वणा ।\nएवमन्यानि चापानि बहूनि कृतहस्तवत् ।\nशारद्वतस्य चिच्छेद पाण्डवः परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kunti's son cut that too with a smooth-jointed arrow; so the Pandava, killer of enemy heroes, skillfully cut many other bows of Sharadvat's son."}},{"n":17,"text":"स छिन्नधनुरादाय अथ शक्तिं प्रतापवान् ।\nप्राहिणोत्पाण्डुपुत्राय प्रदीप्तामशनीमिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up his cut bow, the mighty one then hurled a spear at the son of Pandu, like a blazing thunderbolt."}},{"n":18,"text":"तामर्जुनस्तदायान्तीं शक्तिं हेमविभूषिताम् ।\nवियद्गतां महोल्काभां चिच्छेद दशभिः शरैः ।\nसापतद्दशधा छिन्ना भूमौ पार्थेन धीमता ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that gold-adorned spear came flying through the sky, bright like a great meteor, Arjuna cut it with ten arrows, and it fell in ten pieces on the earth, cut by the wise Partha."}},{"n":19,"text":"युगमध्ये तु भल्लैस्तु ततः स सधनुः कृपः ।\nतमाशु निशितैः पार्थं बिभेद दशभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kripa, with a new bow, quickly pierced Partha with ten sharp arrows, aiming at the middle of his yoke with spear arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततः पार्थो महातेजा विशिखानग्नितेजसः ।\nचिक्षेप समरे क्रुद्धस्त्रयोदश शिलाशितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the very radiant Partha, angry in battle, shot thirteen stone-whetted arrows, bright as fire."}},{"n":21,"text":"अथास्य युगमेकेन चतुर्भिश्चतुरो हयान् ।\nषष्ठेन च शिरः कायाच्छरेण रथसारथेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With one he cut the yoke, with four the four horses, with a sixth arrow the charioteer's head from his body,"}},{"n":22,"text":"त्रिभिस्त्रिवेणुं समरे द्वाभ्यामक्षौ महाबलः ।\nद्वादशेन तु भल्लेन चकर्तास्य ध्वजं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"with three the three-part chariot pole, with two the axle, and with a twelfth spear-arrow, mighty Arjuna cut down his banner."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततो वज्रनिकाशेन फल्गुनः प्रहसन्निव ।\nत्रयोदशेनेन्द्रसमः कृपं वक्षस्यताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Phalguna, as if laughing, struck Kripa in the chest with a thirteenth arrow, equal to a thunderbolt, like Indra."}},{"n":24,"text":"स छिन्नधन्वा विरथो हताश्वो हतसारथिः ।\nगदापाणिरवप्लुत्य तूर्णं चिक्षेप तां गदाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His bow cut, chariotless, horseless and without a charioteer, Kripa leapt down mace in hand and quickly hurled that mace."}},{"n":25,"text":"सा तु मुक्ता गदा गुर्वी कृपेण सुपरिष्कृता ।\nअर्जुनेन शरैर्नुन्ना प्रतिमार्गमथागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the heavy mace, well made and thrown by Kripa, was driven back by Arjuna's arrows and returned on its path."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततो योधाः परीप्सन्तः शारद्वतममर्षणम् ।\nसर्वतः समरे पार्थं शरवर्षैरवाकिरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then warriors, wishing to rescue the angry son of Sharadvat, covered Partha on all sides with showers of arrows."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततो विराटस्य सुतः सव्यमावृत्य वाजिनः ।\nयमकं मण्डलं कृत्वा तान्योधान्प्रत्यवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Virata's son turned the horses to the left, made a double circle, and held those warriors back."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः कृपमुपादाय विरथं ते नरर्षभाः ।\nअपाजह्रुर्महावेगाः कुन्तीपुत्राद्धनंजयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those bulls among men took the chariotless Kripa and carried him very swiftly away from Dhananjaya, Kunti's son."}}]}]}